 reverend mcadam's  demise in an echo of his silver age  return captain america was once again  discovered in a block of ice after years  of being assumed killed in the superhero  purge  around the same time alkamax located the  true hammer of thor mjolnir  steve rogers proves worthy and is able  to hoist the hammer thereby becoming a  heroic thor for the era together with  spider-man and a league of other heroes  in 2099 manifest destiny number one they  begin to repair the fallen world of  2099. this one-shot story marks the  original end of the 2099 line as it  sends the universe off on an upbeat note  marvel has typically depicted the  asgardian apocalypse of ragnarok as a  localized event readers have watched the  event destroy asgard and the gods  several times all without doing much  damage to midgard aka earth  but in what if age of ultron number  three earth is not spared  after slaying thor and destroying asgard  the monstrous serpent jormungand then  targets and kills scores of avengers  soon only a handful of heroes still live  as they decide to take on jormungand  despite the incredibly long odds  amazingly their boldness pays off by  taking the fight to jormungand the team  ends up in a position to find mjolnir  amongst the rubble and black widow then  grabs thor's abandoned hammer she's  evidently been made worthy by her time  fighting to forestall the end of  humanity and thus she can hoist the  hammer skyward and become the new god of  thunder while the book only briefly  shows her efforts nick fury's narration  confirms that she indeed carried the day  and rather spectacularly at that  i want you to meet agent romanov  x-men's rogue has been a fan favorite  for so long that newer readers might not  know that she used to run with villains  like the brotherhood of evil mutants  during that time she even took on carol  danvers and permanently absorbed her  abilities like flight and super strength  what if number 66 entitled what if rogue  possessed the powers of thor took  readers back to this era after breaking  out of prison with her fellow  brotherhood members rogue and the other  mutants find the avengers ready to put  them back in their cells rogue absorbs  the powers of thor who falls into a coma  and dies soon after now permanently  possessing the powers of a god rogue  briefly falls into cahoots with loki  persuading her to help him kill odin the  god of mischief mounts a rebellion he  sends rogue and his troops to invade  asgard and things look pretty desperate  until thor approaches rogue on the  astral plane he convinces her that she  can still be a hero regardless of her  past so she accepts her new role as the  goddess of thunder routes loki's forces  and gains acceptance from the gods and  the avengers  in the disney plus animated series what  if the episode what if thor were an only  child sees the god of thunder as an  immortal partier who can also  nonetheless still wield his hammer  without loki to make his life miserable  or inspire him to protect others he's  lived a charmed life devoid of  consequence or responsibility as such he  is a charming but reckless [ __ ] who  hops from planet to planet throwing  parties that are so intense that they  end up ravaging multiple worlds  after thor arrives on earth things  finally start to change when jane foster  helps him see the value of humanity and  captain marvel keeps his destructive  impulses focused on her in the end the  heroes of earth managed to save the  planet in a manner both silly and  logical as it turns out the best way to  stop a man-child in his tracks is by  calling his mother  yes even dc characters can be worthy of  mjolnir during the blockbuster dc versus  marvel event cosmic forces pitted heroes  from both universes against each other  after thor loses his hammer while  battling dc's captain marvel wonder  woman then comes across mjolnir she's  able to lift it and quickly absorb the  powers of the god of thunder emerging  from the lightning in a new costume  ready for a fight but when her chosen  opponent storm arrives she quickly  discards the hammer in the name of a  fair and honorable fight and promptly  gets wrecked by the mutant  considering that she's fighting for the  very existence of the dc universe it  might seem odd that wonder woman would  so quickly exceed an advantage however  it's worth noting that the results of  the crossover were based on fan voting  so perhaps the creators felt it was far  too unrealistic to give storm her fan a  firm victory over wonder woman when the  justice leaguer had both her own power  and thor's  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite superheroes are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]
 

